  "reason": "RNA-only multiprofile models, especially scvi_n200 with avgpool/transformer, are currently strongest, showing that multiprofile aggregation can help. In contrast, both image-only single-profile encoders are weak (ResNet50 ~0.208, ViT-L ~0.227), and no image-only multiprofile result is available. config_014 tests whether the better single-profile image encoder (ViT-L) improves under multiprofile avgpool aggregation, using a clean one-factor extension from config_013. This is the best next use of budget because it reduces key uncertainty about whether the image modality has any usable signal before spending experiments on multimodal fusion; if image-only multiprofile remains weak, multimodal models are less likely to help, while if it improves, a subsequent multimodal scvi+ViT experiment becomes much more interpretable."
}

